The API reference lists implemented functions and types. These guides explain common modding tasks, their requirements, and the flow between a manifest and Lua code.

== Guides by task ==

* '''Settings:''' declare values in <code>extended.mod.json</code> and read them with <code>shroudforge.settings.get</code>.
* '''Modloader actions:''' connect an action ID to <code>shroudforge.ui.on_action</code>.
* '''Notifications:''' publish notices with <code>shroudforge.notifications.publish</code>.
* '''Logging:''' write useful messages to the ShroudForge log.
* '''Files and exports:''' review package files and export capabilities.
* '''Runtime:''' understand lifecycle callbacks, client and server targets, and native support.
* '''Game state:''' detect the main menu with <code>runtime.is_main_menu()</code> and read the selected local character name with <code>runtime.player.name()</code>.
* '''Localization:''' translate mod text and settings with the localization functions.

Use the [https://bonsaibauer.github.io/shroudforge/ ShroudForge documentation and API reference] for the full current list of functions. API functions may be EML-specific or ShroudForge-specific.

